**Claim 1.** A method for manufacturing an insulated pipe assembly, comprising the steps of:

fixing a jacket pipe within a guide channel;

inserting an insulated inner pipe into the fixed jacket pipe;

applying an overpressure to the insulated inner pipe so as to compress the insulation thereof;

displacing the compressed insulated inner pipe toward a rear end of the jacket pipe; and

releasing the overpressure so as to fix the insulated inner pipe relative to the jacket pipe, thereby forming the insulated pipe assembly.
